    "## R7. Forward Algorithm and Observation Sequence Probability\n",
    "\n",
    "With the HMM parameters (STATES, OBSERVATIONS, pi_0, P, and E) defined, we implement the *Forward Algorithm* (forward_algorithm) to compute the exact probability of observing a given sequence of outcomes (obs_seq) over time. Instead of enumerating every possible hidden state path individually, the algorithm accumulates forward variables (alpha) step by step from t = 0 to T_len - 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Forward Algorithm Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "In *Initialization (t = 0)*, we compute the probability of starting in hidden state j and observing the first outcome obs_seq[0]:\n",
    "\n",
    "alpha[0, j] = pi_0[j] * E[j, obs_0]\n",
    "\n",
    "In *Induction (t from 1 to T_len - 1)*, for each step t and state j, we sum the incoming weighted probabilities from all previous states i using transition matrix P, then multiply by the emission probability of observing obs_t from state j:\n",
    "\n",
    "alpha[t, j] = sum_i(alpha[t - 1, i] * P[i, j]) * E[j, obs_t]\n",
    "\n",
    "In *Termination*, we sum the final forward variables alpha[-1] across all hidden states to obtain the total probability of the entire observation sequence (prob_obs):\n",
    "\n",
    "prob_obs = sum_j(alpha[-1, j])\n",
    "\n",
    "### Sequence Evaluation and Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Applying forward_algorithm to the sample observation sequence [\"High Score\", \"Average Score\", \"Low / Missed\", \"Low / Missed\"] gives a total sequence probability of *P(Observation Sequence) = 0.011057* (about 1.11%).\n",
    "\n",
    "A probability around 0.011057 is expected for one specific four-step sequence because total probability mass is spread across all possible sequences of that length. Along the sequence, the initial High Score supports Focused, the Average Score shifts attention toward Distracted, and the two consecutive Low / Missed observations at the end push substantial probability weight toward Burned Out"
   ]
